<script module>
  import Demo from "$ui/components/Demo.abide"
  import IdentityDemo from "$ui/demos/platform/identity/IdentityDemo.abide"
</script>

<main class="page">
  <h1>Identity</h1>
  <p class="lead"><code>identity()</code> is the current principal — never null, and <strong>isomorphic</strong>: the same import answers in a handler and in a component, where it returns what the server resolved for this page (seeded at hydration, reactive). It starts anonymous; <code>identity.set()</code> promotes it and the router seals a rolling cookie so it persists across requests. A browser cannot seal a cookie, so it cannot promote itself — <code>identity.refresh()</code> re-asks the server after a login mutation. Log in, then watch BOTH lines flip.</p>
  <Demo id="identity" title="<code>identity()</code> — principal, log in, log out" server="src/server/rpc/platformIdentity.ts,src/server/rpc/platformLogin.ts,src/server/rpc/platformLogout.ts" client="src/ui/demos/platform/identity/IdentityDemo.abide" tab="server">
    <IdentityDemo />
  </Demo>
  <aside class="aside">
    <p>The principal in one loop. The read calls <code>identity()</code>; <code>login()</code> is a mutation that calls <code>identity.set()</code> server-side, and re-reading over a fresh request — now carrying the sealed <code>abide-identity</code> cookie — proves the authenticated principal survived the round trip. <code>logout()</code> puts it back to anonymous.</p>
  </aside>
</main>
